course: dictionary
lesson: 13179
title: Freaky and strange
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Freaky is an informal word, the kind people use in everyday talk and stories. It means strange, a bit scary or weird. «The old house made a freaky creaking noise at night.» The noise is odd and gives you a shiver, so freaky fits. Check by swapping in strange: the sentence still works.
explain: Freaky can also mean very unusual and surprising, like a chance that nobody planned. «Sam and Ali both wore the same red hat. That is a freaky coincidence!» A coincidence is when two things happen together by chance, and freaky shows how surprising it is.
explain: Look at the words around freaky to find out which meaning it has. Is the thing scary and weird, or just surprising? The clues tell you. Because freaky is informal, you will hear it in talk and stories more than in school writing.
fact: Freaky is an informal word, used in everyday talk and stories.
fact: «Freaky» means strange and a bit scary or weird.
fact: «Freaky» can also mean very unusual and surprising, as in «a freaky coincidence».
fact: Phrases like «that's freaky» are common in speech.
fact: «Freaky Friday» is a famous film about a mother and daughter who swap bodies.
exercise: «The sky went green and the wind began to howl. It was freaky.» What does freaky mean here? | Made of paper | *Strange and a bit scary | Lovely and warm | Very sleepy
exercise: «Sam and Ali got the same letter on the same day. That is a freaky coincidence!» What does freaky mean in this sentence? | Very slow | *Very unusual and surprising | Full of cold water | Loud and rude
exercise: Find and copy the word that means strange in «The freaky mask grinned at me.» | grinned | *freaky | mask | me
test: Mia says, «That's freaky!» when the lights flicker in a spooky room. What does she mean? | Cold and wet | Very hungry | Bright and shiny | *Strange and a bit scary
test: Which word is the comparing form of freaky, meaning even stranger? | freaker | *freakier | freakyest | freakiest
exam: When a friend says «That is a freaky coincidence», what does freaky mean? | Loud and rude | Strange and scary | *Very unusual and surprising | Very tired
